  "worked_solution": "We notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2\\times 2:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={BA}_{2\\times 2}\n$$",
